s is significantly associated with a number of proxies for incentives to meet privately with investors. Second, we find that roadshows exhibit significantly greater abnormal stock market reactions and analyst forecast activity than other flight windows. Finally, we show that roadshows are associated with greater absolute changes in local institutional ownership, as well as with positive trading gains in firms with high uncertainty and with fewer prior flights to the area. Overall, our evidence suggests that these private meetings are an important information event for the participating investors, who potentially gain an advantage over nonparticipating investors who have no public notice of the meetings.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.2141878","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2012,9,12]],"date-time":"2012-09-12T11:04:38Z","timestamp":1347447878000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":13,"title":["Corporate Jets and Private Meetings with Investors"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"given":"Brian J.","family":"Bushee","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-3549-3012","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Joseph","family":"Gerakos","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Lian Fen","family":"Lee","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"78","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,12]],"date-time":"2026-08-12T15:01:42Z","timestamp":1786546902000},"score":28.732101,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ssrn.com\/abstract=2141878"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2012]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.2141878","published":{"date-parts":[[2012]]},"subtype":"preprint"}],"items-per-page":3,"query":{"start-index":0,"search-terms":null}}}